20.9 Roman numerals
Roman numerals appear in government records more often than we may think. Schedules of an Act, classes of posts and parts of a report are often numbered this way. To match Roman numerals, rebus has a constant ROMAN and a function roman(lo, hi).

# Schedule numbers typed in a register, valid and invalid
schedule_nos &lt;- c("VII", "IV", "XIL", "IIII", "XL", "MCD")
# Find valid Roman numerals
str_view(schedule_nos, exactly(roman()), match = NA)

[1] │ &lt;VII&gt;
[2] │ &lt;IV&gt;
[3] │ XIL
[4] │ IIII
